;; Proof: jumping into a block from below. ESC quits.
;;
;; WHERE THIS HAS GOT TO. Two earlier rounds, both negative, and both worth
;; keeping because they removed suspects:
;;
;;   Round 1, block BESIDE him at the row his feet are on: 0 shoves over 180
;;   ticks. The foot check's obstruction branch needs (playerY mod 16) >= 5, and
;;   rising off a floor-aligned block he always arrives at residue 0, so the
;;   landing branch wins and he stands on the block.
;;
;;   Round 2, block ABOVE him, six geometries (one, two and three tiles up, in
;;   the column that covers his head probe and in the column one tile to its
;;   left): 0 shoves and 0 camera moves over 540 ticks, with playerX unchanged on
;;   every tick of every run. So neither ImpedePlayerMove nor either of
;;   UpdatePlayerCamera{}'s clamps is what a recording shows at a standstill.
;;
;; WHAT ROUND 2 DID ESTABLISH, which round 3 builds on:
;;
;;   - The head check is right. It fires only when the block is in his head
;;     column, and it stops him there; with the block one tile to the left it
;;     never fires, because a single probe at x+8 cannot see it. That is the
;;     ROM's geometry too, and it is why he can pass a block's row at all.
;;   - The ROM's second side row -- playerY-8, standing-big Y+8 -- is solid for
;;     3 or 4 ticks while he rises past such a block, and the engine cannot see
;;     it because it models one side row. Measured, not assumed. Whether the ROM
;;     would have acted on it is a separate question, since DoPlayerSideCheck is
;;     only reached with horizontal movement; that is delta 7, not this.
;;   - He lands standing on the block, 16 px above where he started, which is
;;     what "up to about half past the block" looks like from outside.
;;
;; WHAT ROUND 3 ADDS, AND WHY. Both earlier rounds started him at a standstill,
;; and a recording does not: he was moving when he jumped, because he ran to the
;; spot. That changes two things, and both are candidates for a sideways yank
;; with nothing held afterwards.
;;
;;   1. CheckPlayerSides{} was gated on the pixels moved that tick <> 0 (the global
;;      that held it, playerScrollPixels, has since been deleted), so with speed it
;;      is the only path that can call ImpedePlayerMove{} -- and its push is
;;      keyed on playerMovingDirection, which is a sign, not a side. Running right
;;      into a block on the right asks for a leftward push while his motion sign
;;      is positive. That is a visible yank backwards, and it is precisely the
;;      case the main project's PLAYER_HITBOX note section 4.8 says the ROM refuses at ExIPM ("bails
;;      if the push would reverse the current motion sign"). Delta 9 calls that
;;      closed and the engine does not implement it.
;;   2. The camera scrolls while playerScreenX >= #MARIO_SCREEN_X and
;;      playerSpeedX > 0, and it is recorded per tick here. A camera that scrolls
;;      while he holds nothing moves the whole scene one way and him the other,
;;      which from outside is indistinguishable from being pulled. Worth ruling
;;      in or out before blaming collision code.
;;
;; So each run carries an initial playerSpeedX of 0, +16 or -16 -- 1 px per tick
;; either way -- and nothing else is held from the first tick. The runs are
;; listed explicitly below rather than generated, and each one's parameters are
;; stored in runRow/runCol/runSpeed at the call site so the report cannot
;; mislabel a run. It did, in round 2: the label was recomputed from the slot
;; number with `slot/2`, and an untyped For variable is a float in AmiBlitz, so
;; that division is a float division and the truncation lands on the whole
;; expression at the .w store. MetatileAt{} is unaffected -- pixelX is a .w
;; parameter, so its division is integer division and truncates -- but the
;; lesson stands: never derive a label from an untyped For counter.
;;
;; Reading a trace line: run, tick, x, y, spdY, spdX, dir, camX, flags. Flags
;; are raw bits: 2 head row solid, 4 the unmodelled upper side row solid, 8 the
;; push went right, 16 the push went left, 32 the player and the camera moved
;; together, which is a clamp rather than a push.

WBStartup

#PLAYFIELD_PLANES = 4
#COPPER_FLAGS = $10004
#COPPER_COLORS = 16

#TRACE_TICKS = 90
#RUN_COUNT = 10
#TRACE_SLOTS = #RUN_COUNT*#TRACE_TICKS
#FLOOR_ROW = 12
#HEAD_COLUMN = 9
#LEFT_COLUMN = 8
#RIGHT_COLUMN = 10
#START_X = 138

XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.level.meta.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.areas.table.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.look.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.constants.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.physics.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.palettes.data.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.globals.ab3"
Dim metatileBuffer.w(#MAP_CELLS - 1)
Dim mapBuffer.w(#MAP_CELLS - 1)
Dim mapBufferBackup.w(#MAP_CELLS - 1)
Dim stampHead.w(#STAMP_GID_MAX)
Dim stampNext.w(#MAP_CELLS - 1)
Dim backStampHead.w(#STAMP_GID_MAX)
Dim backStampNext.w(#BACK_CELLS - 1)
Dim metatileBufferBackup.w(#MAP_CELLS - 1)
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.metatile.classes.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.sound.data.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.sound.ab3"

;; Standing height, and it needs #TILE from the include above, so it cannot sit
;; with the rest of the literal block. Standing on row #FLOOR_ROW's floor puts
;; his feet at that row's top and his origin 16 px above it.
#START_Y = (#FLOOR_ROW - 1)*#TILE

;; The ROM's second side row for the standing-big set, rebased: Y+8 in the 32-px
;; envelope is playerY - 8 here. The engine probes only #PROBE_SIDE_Y (= Y+24).
#UPPER_SIDE_DY = -8

Dim traceX0.w(#TRACE_SLOTS - 1)
Dim traceX1.w(#TRACE_SLOTS - 1)
Dim traceY.w(#TRACE_SLOTS - 1)
Dim traceSpdY.w(#TRACE_SLOTS - 1)
Dim traceSpdX.w(#TRACE_SLOTS - 1)
Dim traceDir.w(#TRACE_SLOTS - 1)
Dim traceCamX0.w(#TRACE_SLOTS - 1)
Dim traceCamX1.w(#TRACE_SLOTS - 1)
Dim traceFlags.w(#TRACE_SLOTS - 1)
Dim runRow.w(#RUN_COUNT - 1)
Dim runCol.w(#RUN_COUNT - 1)
Dim runSpeed.w(#RUN_COUNT - 1)
Dim sumShoves.w(#RUN_COUNT - 1)
Dim sumPushLeft.w(#RUN_COUNT - 1)
Dim sumPushRight.w(#RUN_COUNT - 1)
Dim sumPixels.w(#RUN_COUNT - 1)
Dim sumFirstShove.w(#RUN_COUNT - 1)
Dim sumClamps.w(#RUN_COUNT - 1)
Dim sumCamMoves.w(#RUN_COUNT - 1)
Dim sumHeadSolid.w(#RUN_COUNT - 1)
Dim sumUpperSolid.w(#RUN_COUNT - 1)
Dim sumLowestY.w(#RUN_COUNT - 1)
Dim sumFinalY.w(#RUN_COUNT - 1)
Dim sumFinalX.w(#RUN_COUNT - 1)

mapWidth.w = #MAP_W
quitFlag.w = False
screenHeight = DispHeight

InitPalette 0, #COPPER_COLORS
AGAPalRGB 0, 0, 0, 0, 0
AGAPalRGB 0, 1, 120, 120, 120
AGAPalRGB 0, 2, 220, 0, 0
AGAPalRGB 0, 3, 0, 200, 0
AGAPalRGB 0, 4, 60, 60, 60
AGAPalRGB 0, 5, 252, 252, 252
AGAPalRGB 0, 6, 252, 152, 56
BitMap 1, #VIEW_W, screenHeight, #PLAYFIELD_PLANES

BLITZ
;; Canonical DisplayLib startup. $10004 is agacolors + four bitplanes; the extra
;; $10 of $10014 is #smoothscrolling, which the guide says to set only for a
;; scrolling bitmap and which blacks out a non-scrolling one.
InitCopList 0, #COPPER_FLAGS
CreateDisplay 0
DisplayPalette 0, 0
BlitzKeys On

XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.beam.blitz.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.sound.blitz.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.timing-marks.blitz.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.allstars-palette.data.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.map.blitz.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.object-system.blitz.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.debris.blitz.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.floaters.blitz.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.collision.blitz.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.player-state.blitz.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.life.blitz.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.enemies.blitz.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.fireballs.blitz.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.levelend.blitz.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.pipes.blitz.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.object-system-runtime.blitz.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.player.blitz.ab3"
XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.hud.blitz.ab3"

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------
;; Harness
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------

;; Copied from tests/test-harness.ab3 so the two drive the tick identically.
;; If UpdatePlayer{} gains or reorders a call, this has to change with it.
Statement Tick{buttons.w}
  SHARED playerButtons, playerButtonsLast, playerRunningTimer
  SHARED sideCollisionTimer, blockBounceTimer, playerOnGround, playerState
  SHARED playerIsBig, playerCollisionBits
  ;; Not reset here: ApplyCollisionButtonMask{} needs the previous frame's
  ;; mask to survive until it is applied, so the reset is after that call.
  ;; Pole/resize branches below reset explicitly before returning.
  UpdateFlag{}
  If playerState = #PLAYER_ST_POLE
    UpdatePoleSlide{}
    playerButtonsLast = playerButtons
    playerCollisionBits = $ff
    Statement Return
  EndIf
  If playerState = #PLAYER_ST_RESIZE
    UpdateResize{}
    playerButtonsLast = playerButtons
    playerCollisionBits = $ff
    Statement Return
  EndIf
  If playerRunningTimer > 0 Then playerRunningTimer = playerRunningTimer - 1
  If sideCollisionTimer > 0 Then sideCollisionTimer = sideCollisionTimer - 1
  If blockBounceTimer > 0 Then blockBounceTimer = blockBounceTimer - 1
  playerButtons = buttons
  ApplyCollisionButtonMask{}
  playerCollisionBits = $ff
  SetPlayerAbsoluteSpeed{}
  TryStartJump{}
  SetupHorizontalLimits{}
  PrepareGroundMotion{}
  SetPlayerAbsoluteSpeed{}
  ApplyPlayerFacing{}
  ApplyHorizontalFriction{}
  MovePlayerHorizontal{}
  SetPlayerMovingDirection{}
  CheckPlayerSides{}
  SetPlayerAbsoluteSpeed{}
  SelectVerticalForce{}
  If playerOnGround = False Then MovePlayerVertical{}
  CheckPlayerFeet{}
  CheckPlayerHead{}
  UpdatePlayerCamera{}
  UpdatePlayerBoundBox{}
  SetPlayerAbsoluteSpeed{}
  UpdatePlayerAnimation{}
  CheckFlagpole{}
  playerButtonsLast = playerButtons
End Statement

Statement ClearTestMap{}
  SHARED metatileBuffer()
  For testCell = 0 To #MAP_CELLS - 1
    metatileBuffer(testCell) = 0
  Next
End Statement

Statement SetTestCell{testRow.w, testColumn.w, testClass.w}
  SHARED metatileBuffer()
  metatileBuffer(testRow*#MAP_W + testColumn) = testClass
End Statement

Statement SetTestRun{testRow.w, firstColumn.w, lastColumn.w, testClass.w}
  For runColumn = firstColumn To lastColumn
    SetTestCell{testRow, runColumn, testClass}
  Next
End Statement

;; Mirrors tests/test-harness.ab3's PlacePlayer{} -- it has to, because that
;; one is the reason a player placed away from the start is not dragged back to
;; the left edge -- and adds the two things this proof needs: big Mario, and an
;; initial horizontal speed. Size is a single flag, playerIsBig, which is the
;; whole of what the collision path reads.
Statement PlaceBigPlayer{startX.w, startY.w, startSpeed.w}
  SHARED playerX, playerY, playerFacing, playerFrame, playerAnimTimer
  SHARED playerAnimPeriod, playerOnGround, playerButtons, playerButtonsLast
  SHARED playerSpeedX, playerMoveForceX, playerFractionX, cameraFractionX
  SHARED playerSpeedY, playerMoveForceY, playerFractionY, playerVerticalForce, playerFallForce
  SHARED playerSpeedAbsolute, playerRunningTimer, playerRunningSpeed
  SHARED playerMovingDirection, playerFacingDirection
  SHARED playerScreenX, playerJumpOriginY, sideCollisionTimer, blockBounceTimer
  SHARED boundBoxLeft, boundBoxTop, boundBoxRight, boundBoxBottom
  SHARED cameraX, cameraMaxX
  SHARED playerState, playerPoleTimer, flagState, flagX, flagY, playerIsBig
  playerX = startX
  playerY = startY
  playerFacing = #MARIO_FACE_RIGHT
  playerFrame = #MARIO_F_IDLE
  playerAnimTimer = 0
  playerAnimPeriod = #MARIO_ANIM_SLOW
  playerOnGround = True
  playerButtons = 0
  playerButtonsLast = 0
  playerSpeedX = startSpeed
  playerMoveForceX = 0
  playerFractionX = 0
  cameraFractionX = 0
  playerSpeedY = 0
  playerMoveForceY = 0
  playerFractionY = 0
  playerVerticalForce = 0
  playerFallForce = 0
  playerSpeedAbsolute = 0
  playerRunningTimer = 0
  playerRunningSpeed = 0
  playerMovingDirection = #MARIO_BTN_RIGHT
  playerFacingDirection = #MARIO_BTN_RIGHT
  playerScreenX = startX
  playerJumpOriginY = startY
  sideCollisionTimer = 0
  blockBounceTimer = 0
  boundBoxLeft = playerX + #BOUND_LEFT
  boundBoxTop = playerY + #BOUND_TOP
  boundBoxRight = playerX + #BOUND_RIGHT
  boundBoxBottom = playerY + #BOUND_BOTTOM
  cameraX = 0
  cameraMaxX = 0
  playerState = #PLAYER_ST_FREE
  playerPoleTimer = 0
  flagState = #FLAG_ST_IDLE
  flagX = (#FLAGPOLE_X/#TILE)*#TILE + #FLAGPOLE_SHAFT_X - #FLAG_W + 1
  flagY = #FLAGPOLE_Y + #FLAG_TOP_DY
  playerIsBig = True
End Statement

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------
;; The runs
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------

Statement RunScenario{blockRow.w, blockColumn.w, startSpeed.w, slot.w}
  SHARED traceX0(), traceX1(), traceY(), traceSpdY(), traceSpdX()
  SHARED traceDir(), traceCamX0(), traceCamX1(), traceFlags()
  SHARED runRow(), runCol(), runSpeed()
  SHARED sumShoves(), sumPushLeft(), sumPushRight(), sumPixels()
  SHARED sumFirstShove(), sumClamps(), sumCamMoves()
  SHARED sumHeadSolid(), sumUpperSolid(), sumLowestY(), sumFinalY(), sumFinalX()
  SHARED playerX, playerY, playerSpeedX, playerSpeedY, playerMovingDirection
  SHARED cameraX
  slotBase.w = slot*#TRACE_TICKS
  runRow(slot) = blockRow
  runCol(slot) = blockColumn
  runSpeed(slot) = startSpeed
  ClearTestMap{}
  SetTestRun{#FLOOR_ROW, 0, #MAP_W - 1, #MT_GROUND}
  SetTestCell{blockRow, blockColumn, #MT_BLOCK}
  PlaceBigPlayer{#START_X, #START_Y, startSpeed}
  sumShoves(slot) = 0
  sumPushLeft(slot) = 0
  sumPushRight(slot) = 0
  sumPixels(slot) = 0
  sumFirstShove(slot) = -1
  sumClamps(slot) = 0
  sumCamMoves(slot) = 0
  sumHeadSolid(slot) = 0
  sumUpperSolid(slot) = 0
  sumLowestY(slot) = 32767
  For traceTick = 0 To #TRACE_TICKS - 1
    traceIndex.w = slotBase + traceTick
    traceX0(traceIndex) = playerX
    traceY(traceIndex) = playerY
    traceSpdY(traceIndex) = playerSpeedY
    traceSpdX(traceIndex) = playerSpeedX
    traceDir(traceIndex) = playerMovingDirection
    traceCamX0(traceIndex) = cameraX
    traceFlags(traceIndex) = 0
    ;; Sampled before the tick, so these are the rows the tick is about to read.
    If MetatileAt{playerX + #PROBE_TOP_X, playerY + #PROBE_TOP_Y_BIG} <> #MT_EMPTY
      traceFlags(traceIndex) = traceFlags(traceIndex) OR 2
      sumHeadSolid(slot) = sumHeadSolid(slot) + 1
    EndIf
    upperSolid.w = False
    If MetatileAt{playerX + #PROBE_SIDE_X1, playerY + #UPPER_SIDE_DY} <> #MT_EMPTY Then upperSolid = True
    If MetatileAt{playerX + #PROBE_SIDE_X2, playerY + #UPPER_SIDE_DY} <> #MT_EMPTY Then upperSolid = True
    If upperSolid = True
      traceFlags(traceIndex) = traceFlags(traceIndex) OR 4
      sumUpperSolid(slot) = sumUpperSolid(slot) + 1
    EndIf
    Tick{#MARIO_BTN_JUMP}
    traceX1(traceIndex) = playerX
    traceCamX1(traceIndex) = cameraX
    If playerX < traceX0(traceIndex)
      traceFlags(traceIndex) = traceFlags(traceIndex) OR 16
      sumShoves(slot) = sumShoves(slot) + 1
      sumPushLeft(slot) = sumPushLeft(slot) + 1
      sumPixels(slot) = sumPixels(slot) + traceX0(traceIndex) - playerX
      If sumFirstShove(slot) < 0 Then sumFirstShove(slot) = traceTick
    EndIf
    If playerX > traceX0(traceIndex)
      traceFlags(traceIndex) = traceFlags(traceIndex) OR 8
      sumShoves(slot) = sumShoves(slot) + 1
      sumPushRight(slot) = sumPushRight(slot) + 1
    EndIf
    If cameraX <> traceCamX0(traceIndex)
      traceFlags(traceIndex) = traceFlags(traceIndex) OR 32
      sumCamMoves(slot) = sumCamMoves(slot) + 1
      sumPixels(slot) = sumPixels(slot) + cameraX - traceCamX0(traceIndex)
    EndIf
    If playerX <> traceX0(traceIndex) AND cameraX = traceCamX0(traceIndex)
      sumClamps(slot) = sumClamps(slot) + 1
    EndIf
    If playerY < sumLowestY(slot) Then sumLowestY(slot) = playerY
  Next
  sumFinalX(slot) = playerX
  sumFinalY(slot) = playerY
End Statement

Statement DrawTrace{slot.w, baseY.w}
  SHARED traceFlags()
  Use BitMap 1
  For drawTick = 0 To #TRACE_TICKS - 1
    drawIndex.w = slot*#TRACE_TICKS + drawTick
    drawPen.w = 4
    If (traceFlags(drawIndex) AND 4) <> 0 Then drawPen = 3
    If (traceFlags(drawIndex) AND 2) <> 0 Then drawPen = 5
    If (traceFlags(drawIndex) AND 62) <> 0 Then drawPen = 2
    Boxf 4 + drawTick*3, baseY, 6 + drawTick*3, baseY + 8, drawPen
  Next
End Statement

Statement DrawGeometry{}
  SHARED metatileBuffer()
  Use BitMap 1
  ;; Only the visible columns: the buffer is the whole 224-wide level, and
  ;; stamping all of it every frame is 3360 Boxf calls for nothing.
  For drawRow = 0 To #MAP_H - 1
    For drawColumn = 0 To #VIEW_TILES_W - 1
      If metatileBuffer(drawRow*#MAP_W + drawColumn) > 0
        Boxf drawColumn*#TILE, drawRow*#TILE, drawColumn*#TILE + #TILE - 1, drawRow*#TILE + #TILE - 1, 1
      EndIf
    Next
  Next
  Boxf #LEFT_COLUMN*#TILE, #FLOOR_ROW*#TILE, #LEFT_COLUMN*#TILE + #TILE - 1, #FLOOR_ROW*#TILE + #TILE - 1, 6
  Boxf #RIGHT_COLUMN*#TILE, #FLOOR_ROW*#TILE, #RIGHT_COLUMN*#TILE + #TILE - 1, #FLOOR_ROW*#TILE + #TILE - 1, 6
  Boxf #START_X + #PROBE_SIDE_X1, #START_Y + #PROBE_SIDE_Y, #START_X + #PROBE_SIDE_X2, #START_Y + #PROBE_SIDE_Y, 3
  Boxf #START_X + #PROBE_FOOT_X1, #START_Y + #PROBE_FOOT_Y, #START_X + #PROBE_FOOT_X2, #START_Y + #PROBE_FOOT_Y, 3
  Boxf #START_X + #PROBE_TOP_X, #START_Y + #PROBE_TOP_Y_BIG, #START_X + #PROBE_TOP_X, #START_Y + #PROBE_TOP_Y_BIG, 5
End Statement

;; Two controls at rest, then the four "moving into a block" cases, then the
;; four "moving away from it" cases, then the ordinary bump taken at speed.
RunScenario{#FLOOR_ROW - 1, #LEFT_COLUMN, 0, 0}
RunScenario{#FLOOR_ROW - 2, #LEFT_COLUMN, 0, 1}
RunScenario{#FLOOR_ROW - 2, #LEFT_COLUMN, 16, 2}
RunScenario{#FLOOR_ROW - 2, #LEFT_COLUMN, -16, 3}
RunScenario{#FLOOR_ROW - 2, #RIGHT_COLUMN, 16, 4}
RunScenario{#FLOOR_ROW - 2, #RIGHT_COLUMN, -16, 5}
RunScenario{#FLOOR_ROW - 3, #RIGHT_COLUMN, 16, 6}
RunScenario{#FLOOR_ROW - 3, #RIGHT_COLUMN, -16, 7}
RunScenario{#FLOOR_ROW - 3, #HEAD_COLUMN, 16, 8}
RunScenario{#FLOOR_ROW - 3, #LEFT_COLUMN, 0, 9}

While quitFlag = False
  Use BitMap 1
  Cls 0
  DrawGeometry{}
  For showSlot = 0 To #RUN_COUNT - 1
    DrawTrace{showSlot, 60 + showSlot*10}
  Next
  VWait
  DisplayBitMap 0, 1
  If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_ESC) Then quitFlag = True
Wend

AMIGA
If WriteFile(0, "sparky-dave:game/proofs/results/jump-into-block-results.txt")
  FileOutput 0
  NPrint "Jump into block from below: sideways movement with nothing held"
  NPrint ""
  NPrint "big Mario at x", #START_X, "y", #START_Y, "feet on the floor at row", #FLOOR_ROW
  NPrint "jump held every tick,", #TRACE_TICKS, "ticks per run,", #RUN_COUNT, "runs"
  NPrint "flags: 2 head solid  4 unmodelled upper side solid  8 pushed right"
  NPrint "16 pushed left  32 player and camera moved together"
  NPrint ""
  For reportSlot = 0 To #RUN_COUNT - 1
    NPrint "run", reportSlot, ": block row", runRow(reportSlot), "column", runCol(reportSlot), "speedX", runSpeed(reportSlot)
    NPrint "  shoves", sumShoves(reportSlot), "left", sumPushLeft(reportSlot), "right", sumPushRight(reportSlot), "px", sumPixels(reportSlot), "first tick", sumFirstShove(reportSlot)
    NPrint "  camera moved ticks", sumCamMoves(reportSlot), "clamps", sumClamps(reportSlot), "head solid", sumHeadSolid(reportSlot), "upper side solid", sumUpperSolid(reportSlot)
    NPrint "  lowest y", sumLowestY(reportSlot), "final x", sumFinalX(reportSlot), "final y", sumFinalY(reportSlot)
  Next
  NPrint ""
  NPrint "run tick x y spdY spdX dir camX head upper push"
  For reportSlot = 0 To #RUN_COUNT - 1
    reportBase.w = reportSlot*#TRACE_TICKS
    For reportTick = 0 To #TRACE_TICKS - 1
      reportFlags.w = traceFlags(reportBase + reportTick)
      reportHead.w = (reportFlags AND 2)/2
      reportUpper.w = (reportFlags AND 4)/4
      reportPush.w = (reportFlags AND 24) + ((reportFlags AND 32)/32)*64
      NPrint reportSlot, reportTick, traceX1(reportBase + reportTick), traceY(reportBase + reportTick)
      NPrint "  spdY", traceSpdY(reportBase + reportTick), "spdX", traceSpdX(reportBase + reportTick), "dir", traceDir(reportBase + reportTick)
      NPrint "  camX", traceCamX1(reportBase + reportTick), "head", reportHead, "upper", reportUpper, "push", reportPush
    Next
  Next
  CloseFile 0
EndIf
End
